    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0706, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5547\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to directing the commissioner of environmental conservation to\ncreate gift cards for hunting and fishing licenses\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo require the Commissioner of the Department of Environmental Conserva-\ntion (DEC) to promulgate rules and regulations establishing gift cards\nfor hunting and fishing licenses in New York State.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 11-0706 of the environmental conservation law\nto require the Commissioner of the Department of Environmental Conserva-\ntion (DEC) to promulgate rules and regulations establishing gift cards\nfor New York State hunting and fishing licenses.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe state budget for fiscal year 2012-2013 authorized the commissioner\nto establish gift cards for hunting and fishing, however no gift cards\nhave been made since this became law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation requires the Commissioner of the Department of Environ-\nmental Conservation to promulgate rules and regulations establishing\ngift cards for hunting and fishing licenses in New York State. Similar\ngift cards, used for camping and entrance into state parks, already\nexist. Like those programs, hunting and fishing license gift cards will\npromote the industry and generate revenue for the state.\n\nCurrent gift card programs are thriving. Gift cards for camping permits,\noffered by the Office of Parks, may be used for anything from golf\nreservations and greens fees to the purchase of firewood or boat\nrentals, as well as camping site reservations. These camping permit gift\ncards, as well as Empire Passports, which provide free entrance into\nstate parks, are advertised for sale on the web site for the New York\nState Office of Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation.\n\nIn 2013, the New York State Department of Environmental Conservation\n(DEC) began to issue their own gift cards that can be used for camping\nat all New York State Department of Environmental Conservation Facili-\nties. These gifts cards are similar to those offered by the Office of\nParks, but they carry their own restrictions as imposed by the DEC and\nare only for use at DEC facilities.\n\nFollowing the precedent set by both the Office of Parks and the DEC,\nthis legislation seeks to expand the sale of recreational gift cards.\nHunting and fishing are recreations very similar to those activities\ncurrently receiving gift cards and licenses for these activities should\nbe made available through the purchase of gift cards.  This legislation\nwill achieve that goal and should be passed.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-2018: A.723 reported to Ways & Means/S.754 referred to Environ-\nmental Conservation\n2015-2016: A.7467 reported to Ways & Means/S.3106 Passed Senate\n2013-2014: A.1627-A/S.6575 - Veto 529\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nPotential for increased revenue.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
